WEBVTT

NOTE
Timestamps use the original Library of Congress MP3 clock.
See voices.yaml for the excerpt start and end.

billy-mccrea-01
00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.990
<v Uncle Billy McCrea>And the Yankees had come,</v>

billy-mccrea-02
00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:15.560
<v Uncle Billy McCrea>and after a while there'd be a whole troop
of men come,</v>

billy-mccrea-03
00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:20.490
<v Uncle Billy McCrea>they said they was Yankees. All walking, all
walking.</v>

billy-mccrea-04
00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.890
<v Uncle Billy McCrea>That crew of Yankees would go through.</v>

billy-mccrea-05
00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:28.090
<v Uncle Billy McCrea>Next time you see, there come a whole troop
of Yankees,</v>

billy-mccrea-06
00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.670
<v Uncle Billy McCrea>all riding horses,</v>

billy-mccrea-07
00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.540
<v Uncle Billy McCrea>big guns a-hanging on in there, and all like
that you know. Yeah.</v>

billy-mccrea-08
00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:38.610
<v Uncle Billy McCrea>We all would standing looking at them, all
going home.</v>

billy-mccrea-09
00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.620
<v Uncle Billy McCrea>And I said, I ask them, I said, I ask them,
I say,</v>

billy-mccrea-10
00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.340
<v Uncle Billy McCrea>"Mama, where they, where they going?"</v>

billy-mccrea-11
00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:44.950
<v Uncle Billy McCrea>Said, "They all going home now."</v>
